      "id": "overview_17",
      "label": "Ages 8 to 10. The sweet spot. Bike rides, wa...",
      "default": "<strong>Ages 8 to 10.</strong> The sweet spot. Bike rides, walking home, staying after for practice, a friend's house two streets over. Texting and location both get used daily."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "overview_18",
      "label": "Ages 11 to 12. Works well when the answer to...",
      "default": "<strong>Ages 11 to 12.</strong> Works well when the answer to a phone is not yet. The keyboard on JrTrack Pro matters most here."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "overview_19",
      "label": "The watch starts with the basics and lets yo...",
      "default": "The watch starts with the basics and lets you unlock more as they are ready. Apps, 911, and Buddies are all switches you flip, not defaults."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "overview_20",
      "label": "Starts with the basics, grows from there",
      "default": "Starts with the basics, grows from there"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "HALOGPS"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_01",
      "label": "Feature 01",
      "default": "Feature 01"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_02",
      "label": "HaloGPS",
      "default": "HaloGPS"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "halogps_03",
      "label": "Engineered to find them, every time. Multi-c...",
      "default": "Engineered to find them, every time. Multi-constellation GPS, Wi-Fi assist, and live updates every 5 to 10 seconds when you want to watch them move."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "halogps_04",
      "label": "115satellite signals",
      "default": "<b>115</b><span>satellite signals</span>"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "halogps_05",
      "label": "5 to 10 sActive Tracking",
      "default": "<b>5 to 10 s</b><span>Active Tracking</span>"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "halogps_06",
      "label": "92%faster first lock4",
      "default": "<b>92%</b><span>faster first lock<sup>4</sup></span>"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "halogps_07",
      "label": "Wi-Fiassist indoors",
      "default": "<b>Wi-Fi</b><span>assist indoors</span>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_08",
      "label": "How it finds them",
      "default": "How it finds them"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "halogps_09",
      "label": "In shortThe watch listens to 115 satellite s...",
      "default": "<em>In short</em>The watch listens to 115 satellite signals across multiple constellations at once, instead of one network. Losing a few signals to a rooftop or a tree line does not cost the fix."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "halogps_10",
      "label": "An older single-network GPS chip needs a cle...",
      "default": "An older single-network GPS chip needs a clear view of a handful of satellites. Downtown, under trees, or in a school corridor, that is a hard ask, and the result is the wandering dot every parent of a first-generation kids watch has complained about."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "halogps_11",
      "label": "HaloGPS pulls from several satellite systems...",
      "default": "HaloGPS pulls from several satellite systems simultaneously, so there are always more signals than it needs. Indoors, Wi-Fi assist uses nearby networks as extra reference points to keep the dot on the right building. In Cosmo lab testing, first lock came about 92 percent faster than single-constellation GPS.<sup>4</sup>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_12",
      "label": "Two kids, one map, in the Cosmo app",
      "default": "Two kids, one map, in the Cosmo app"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_13",
      "label": "Active Tracking",
      "default": "Active Tracking"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "halogps_14",
      "label": "In shortNormally the watch checks in on a sc...",
      "default": "<em>In short</em>Normally the watch checks in on a schedule you set. Tap Active Tracking and it updates every 5 to 10 seconds, for the twenty minutes you actually need it."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "halogps_15",
      "label": "This is the mode for the walk home, the bike...",
      "default": "This is the mode for the walk home, the bike ride to practice, or the ten minutes after a \"where are you?\" text goes unanswered. The map moves with them."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "halogps_16",
      "label": "It is also the single biggest lever on batte...",
      "default": "It is also the single biggest lever on battery life, which is why it is a button rather than a default. Frequent location updates keep the GPS radio awake, and an awake radio drinks. The default schedule and scheduled hours cover a normal day with battery to spare."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "halogps_17",
      "label": "Default schedule. Periodic check-ins, easy o...",
      "default": "<strong>Default schedule.</strong> Periodic check-ins, easy on the battery."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "halogps_18",
      "label": "Scheduled hours. Update more often on the wa...",
      "default": "<strong>Scheduled hours.</strong> Update more often on the walk to school and the walk home, less in between."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "halogps_19",
      "label": "Active Tracking. Every 5 to 10 seconds, on d...",
      "default": "<strong>Active Tracking.</strong> Every 5 to 10 seconds, on demand."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_20",
      "label": "SafeZones",
      "default": "SafeZones"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "halogps_21",
      "label": "A SafeZone is a circle you draw on the map. ...",
      "default": "A SafeZone is a circle you draw on the map. When your child crosses into it or out of it, you get a notification. Most families end up with three or four: home, school, practice, and a grandparent's house."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "halogps_22",
      "label": "Arrival is the alert you will use most. \"Arr...",
      "default": "<strong>Arrival is the alert you will use most.</strong> \"Arrived at school\" at 8:12 a.m. answers the question you were about to ask."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "halogps_23",
      "label": "Draw them a little generous. A zone drawn ti...",
      "default": "<strong>Draw them a little generous.</strong> A zone drawn tight around a building fires more often than one that covers the block, because a GPS fix drifts a little even when your child is standing still."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "halogps_24",
      "label": "HaloGPS makes them faster. Real-time SafeZon...",
      "default": "<strong>HaloGPS makes them faster.</strong> Real-time SafeZone detection means the alert lands when they cross the line, not five minutes later."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_25",
      "label": "Draw the circle, choose the alerts",
      "default": "Draw the circle, choose the alerts"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_26",
      "label": "How accurate it is, by situation",
      "default": "How accurate it is, by situation"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "halogps_27",
      "label": "Accuracy is not one number. It changes with ...",
      "default": "Accuracy is not one number. It changes with where your child is standing, and it helps to know the pattern before you read the map at 3 p.m. on a Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_28",
      "label": "Outdoors, open sky",
      "default": "Outdoors, open sky"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "halogps_29",
      "label": "The best case. Park, field, sidewalk, bike p...",
      "default": "The best case. Park, field, sidewalk, bike path. The dot lands on the right side of the street and stays there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_30",
      "label": "Dense or covered",
      "default": "Dense or covered"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "halogps_31",
      "label": "Tall buildings, heavy tree cover, a parking ...",
      "default": "Tall buildings, heavy tree cover, a parking garage. The fix holds, but expect the dot to settle for a moment."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_32",
      "label": "Deep indoors",
      "default": "Deep indoors"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "halogps_33",
      "label": "The middle of a school, a basement, a big-bo...",
      "default": "The middle of a school, a basement, a big-box store. Wi-Fi assist keeps you at the right building. Expect the building, not the room."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "halogps_34",
      "label": "Read the timestamp, not just the pin. A loca...",
      "default": "<b>Read the timestamp, not just the pin.</b> A location from eleven minutes ago is a different fact from one from eleven seconds ago. The app shows both. If you need the second, start Active Tracking."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_35",
      "label": "Location history",
      "default": "Location history"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "halogps_36",
      "label": "The app keeps the day's trail, so \"where wer...",
      "default": "The app keeps the day's trail, so \"where were they at 4?\" is something you can answer after the fact rather than something you had to be watching for. In practice it gets used for logistics far more than suspicion: confirming the bus ran late, or working out where a coat was left."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "halogps_37",
      "label": "History follows the same accuracy rules as l...",
      "default": "History follows the same accuracy rules as live location. A gap in the trail almost always means no signal or a dead battery."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_38",
      "label": "Questions parents ask about location",
      "default": "Questions parents ask about location"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_39",
      "label": "Can I see where they are all day?",
      "default": "Can I see where they are all day?"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "halogps_40",
      "label": "Yes. Location reports on the schedule you se...",
      "default": "Yes. Location reports on the schedule you set, and the map is in the app whenever you open it. For a live view, Active Tracking updates every 5 to 10 seconds. For \"did they get there\", SafeZone arrival alerts do it without you opening the app at all."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_41",
      "label": "Does location drain the battery?",
      "default": "Does location drain the battery?"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "halogps_42",
      "label": "Update frequency is the biggest factor in ba...",
      "default": "Update frequency is the biggest factor in battery life by a wide margin. The default schedule gets a full day comfortably. Continuous Active Tracking will not. Use it for the stretches you need it, and let scheduled hours cover the rest. <a href=\"#battery\">More on battery</a>."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_43",
      "label": "What if they take the watch off?",
      "default": "What if they take the watch off?"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "halogps_44",
      "label": "The map shows you where the watch is. There ...",
      "default": "The map shows you where the watch is. There is no wear detection, so a watch left at a friend's house shows the friend's house. Watches that go on with shoes in the morning and come off at bedtime stay on wrists; it is a habit more than a feature."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "halogps_45",
      "label": "What happens with no signal?",
      "default": "What happens with no signal?"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "halogps_46",
      "label": "The map holds the last known fix with its ti...",
      "default": "The map holds the last known fix with its timestamp, and catches up when signal returns. Texts sent in the meantime deliver when the watch reconnects, like any SMS."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "SAFECORE"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_01",
      "label": "Feature 02",
      "default": "Feature 02"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_02",
      "label": "SafeCore",
      "default": "SafeCore"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "safecore_03",
      "label": "The safety layer on every JrTrack. SOS to ev...",
      "default": "The safety layer on every JrTrack. SOS to every Guardian with live location, SafeZone alerts, optional 911, and a contact list that keeps everyone else out."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "safecore_04",
      "label": "1 holdto send an SOS",
      "default": "<b>1 hold</b><span>to send an SOS</span>"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "safecore_05",
      "label": "EveryGuardian alerted at once",
      "default": "<b>Every</b><span>Guardian alerted at once</span>"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "safecore_06",
      "label": "911optional, parent-enabled",
      "default": "<b>911</b><span>optional, parent-enabled</span>"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "safecore_07",
      "label": "0unknown numbers get through",
      "default": "<b>0</b><span>unknown numbers get through</span>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_08",
      "label": "What SafeCore includes",
      "default": "What SafeCore includes"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "safecore_09",
      "label": "In shortFour things, on every plan, with not...",
      "default": "<em>In short</em>Four things, on every plan, with nothing behind a higher tier: SOS, SafeZones, optional 911, and approved contacts only."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_10",
      "label": "SOS",
      "default": "SOS"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "safecore_11",
      "label": "A long hold on the side button alerts every ...",
      "default": "A long hold on the side button alerts every parent and Guardian with the child's live location."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_12",
      "label": "SafeZones",
      "default": "SafeZones"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "safecore_13",
      "label": "Arrival and departure alerts for the places ...",
      "default": "Arrival and departure alerts for the places you draw on the map. <a href=\"#safezones\">How they work</a>."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_14",
      "label": "Optional 911",
      "default": "Optional 911"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "safecore_15",
      "label": "Off by default. You turn it on in the app wh...",
      "default": "Off by default. You turn it on in the app when you decide your child is ready for it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_16",
      "label": "What happens when they hold the button",
      "default": "What happens when they hold the button"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_17",
      "label": "The sequence, start to finish.",
      "default": "The sequence, start to finish."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "safecore_18",
      "label": "Your child presses and holds the side button...",
      "default": "Your child presses and holds the side button. On JrTrack Pro, that is the orange Action button."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "safecore_19",
      "label": "The watch takes a fresh location fix rather ...",
      "default": "The watch takes a fresh location fix rather than reusing the last known one."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "safecore_20",
      "label": "Every Guardian on the account is alerted at ...",
      "default": "Every Guardian on the account is alerted at once, not just the primary parent. Nobody has to be awake and holding their phone for the alert to reach the others."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "safecore_21",
      "label": "The alert carries live location, so the map ...",
      "default": "The alert carries live location, so the map keeps updating while your child moves."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "safecore_22",
      "label": "If you have enabled 911, your child can plac...",
      "default": "If you have enabled 911, your child can place that call from the same screen."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "safecore_23",
      "label": "SOS always gets through. School-Fi, Bedtime,...",
      "default": "<b>SOS always gets through.</b> School-Fi, Bedtime, and every other restriction leave it on. There is no mode where the button does nothing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_24",
      "label": "One long hold, every Guardian notified",
      "default": "One long hold, every Guardian notified"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_25",
      "label": "Guardians, and why you want more than one",
      "default": "Guardians, and why you want more than one"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "safecore_26",
      "label": "A Guardian is an adult you invite into the a...",
      "default": "A Guardian is an adult you invite into the account who can see location, receive SOS and SafeZone alerts, read messages, and change settings. A contact can only call and text. The most common setup gap is a single Guardian: one parent, one phone, one point of failure."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "safecore_27",
      "label": "Add both parents, including across a split h...",
      "default": "Add both parents, including across a split household. Alerts reach everyone at once."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "safecore_28",
      "label": "Add the adult who is geographically closest ...",
      "default": "Add the adult who is geographically closest during the school day. A grandparent five minutes away beats a parent forty minutes away."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "safecore_29",
      "label": "The full Guardian-versus-contact breakdown i...",
      "default": "The full Guardian-versus-contact breakdown is in <a href=\"#who-sees\">the Cosmo app chapter</a>."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_30",
      "label": "More adults on the account, more coverage",
      "default": "More adults on the account, more coverage"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_31",
      "label": "911 calling",
      "default": "911 calling"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "safecore_32",
      "label": "In shortIt is off until you turn it on, and ...",
      "default": "<em>In short</em>It is off until you turn it on, and you can turn it back off. That is deliberate."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "safecore_33",
      "label": "A six-year-old with a 911 button on their wr...",
      "default": "A six-year-old with a 911 button on their wrist is a different proposition from an eleven-year-old who walks home alone. So the switch is yours, in the Cosmo app. Most families enable it around the time a child starts travelling a route on their own, after a conversation about what counts as an emergency and what happens on the other end of that call."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_34",
      "label": "Approved contacts only",
      "default": "Approved contacts only"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "safecore_35",
      "label": "In shortThe watch only accepts calls and tex...",
      "default": "<em>In short</em>The watch only accepts calls and texts from numbers on the contact list, and only you can add to that list. Everything else is refused before it rings."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "safecore_36",
      "label": "You add every contact, from the Cosmo app. Y...",
      "default": "<strong>You add every contact,</strong> from the Cosmo app. Your child cannot add one from the watch."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "safecore_37",
      "label": "Inbound is filtered. A wrong number, a spam ...",
      "default": "<strong>Inbound is filtered.</strong> A wrong number, a spam call, a robotext, none of them reach the watch."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "safecore_38",
      "label": "Outbound is limited the same way. The watch ...",
      "default": "<strong>Outbound is limited the same way.</strong> The watch cannot dial a number that is not on the list."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "safecore_39",
      "label": "There is no second door. No email, no social...",
      "default": "<strong>There is no second door.</strong> No email, no social app, no browser, so nothing else to filter."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "safecore_40",
      "label": "Buddies are the one exception, and it still ...",
      "default": "<b>Buddies are the one exception, and it still runs through you.</b> Kids can add each other as Buddies from the watch without swapping phone numbers, but every request waits for your approval. <a href=\"#buddies\">How Buddies work</a>."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_41",
      "label": "Questions parents ask about safety",
      "default": "Questions parents ask about safety"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_42",
      "label": "Is there someone on the other end of an SOS?",
      "default": "Is there someone on the other end of an SOS?"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "safecore_43",
      "label": "The alert goes to you and the Guardians you ...",
      "default": "The alert goes to you and the Guardians you added, not to a Cosmo call center. That is why it pays to add more than one adult, and to include someone who is usually close to your child during the day. Optional 911 covers the case where a real emergency line is needed."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_44",
      "label": "Can a stranger contact my child?",
      "default": "Can a stranger contact my child?"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "safecore_45",
      "label": "No. Inbound calls and texts are accepted onl...",
      "default": "No. Inbound calls and texts are accepted only from the contact list, and only you can add to it. The watch also cannot call or text out to a number that is not on the list."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_46",
      "label": "Does SOS work during School-Fi or Bedtime?",
      "default": "Does SOS work during School-Fi or Bedtime?"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "safecore_47",
      "label": "Yes. Every restriction level leaves SOS on. ...",
      "default": "Yes. Every restriction level leaves SOS on. Location keeps reporting too."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "safecore_48",
      "label": "Does it detect falls or monitor health?",
      "default": "Does it detect falls or monitor health?"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "safecore_49",
      "label": "No. JrTrack is a connection and location dev...",
      "default": "No. JrTrack is a connection and location device, not a medical one. There is no fall detection or heart-rate alerting."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "TEXTING"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "texting_01",
      "label": "Feature 03",
      "default": "Feature 03"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "texting_02",
      "label": "Texting",
      "default": "Texting"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "texting_03",
      "label": "TrueTexting gives the watch a real number an...",
      "default": "TrueTexting gives the watch a real number and real SMS. Photos, videos, voice notes, group chats, and talk to text sit on top of it, and every word is readable in the Cosmo app."
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "texting_04",
      "label": "SMSfrom its own number",
      "default": "<b>SMS</b><span>from its own number</span>"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "texting_05",
      "label": "MMSphotos, video, voice",
      "default": "<b>MMS</b><span>photos, video, voice</span>"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "texting_06",
      "label": "Groupsthe whole family in one thread",
      "default": "<b>Groups</b><span>the whole family in one thread</span>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "texting_07",
      "label": "TrueTexting: real SMS, from a real number",
      "default": "TrueTexting: real SMS, from a real number"
